## Lowering from the typed HIR to the Core IR. Follows `lower.rs` of emela-core.
##
## Unlike the reference, which lowers generic code once and monomorphizes the IR afterwards, Graft
## lowers each instance of a definition separately: a definition with its type arguments, with
## `TyBound(i)` in the types of its body replaced by them as it goes. So every function in the
## module is monomorphic, and showing a value always knows its type.
##
## Only the instances reachable from the roots (the entry's `main`) are lowered: a work list
## starts at the roots, and each reference to a fn adds the instance it needs.
##
## Not lowered yet: traits, errors, effects, suspension, consts. What cannot be lowered is
## reported, and the build stops.
